---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { buildGraph } from '../lib/schema';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/format';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Affiliate disclosure', href: '/affiliate-disclosure/' },
];
const updated = new Date(`${site.policiesUpdated}T00:00:00.000Z`);
const description = 'Satsplain plans to sell its own Safety Kit. No affiliate links today. If one is added, the page where it appears will say so.';
---
<Base title="Affiliate disclosure · Satsplain" description={description} graph={buildGraph({ crumbs })}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="kicker">Money</p>
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p class="lede">Satsplain plans to sell its own Safety Kit. Affiliate links, if we add them, will be labeled where they appear.</p>
    <p class="meta">Updated <time datetime={site.policiesUpdated}>{formatDate(updated)}</time></p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The Federal Trade Commission's Endorsement Guides, at <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-16/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-255">16 CFR Part 255</a>, say a material connection between a marketer and someone who endorses a product should be disclosed clearly when the audience would not expect it. <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-16/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-255/section-255.5">Section 255.5</a> is the disclosure section. The connection has to be hard to miss, not buried.
    </p>
    <p>
      Satsplain plans to sell the <a href="/safety-kit/">Safety Kit</a>, a blank plate the buyer stamps with a seed phrase, together with a punch, a tamper-evident pouch, and a setup card. We have a financial interest in that kit. The product page says so at the top. A guide that mentions the kit says so in the same view. The kit is not for sale yet, and these pages do not name a price.
    </p>
    <p>
      That interest stays separate from the guides. Topics are chosen because a reader needs them. Sources are cited. No article requires a purchase. A paper backup of a seed phrase is a complete alternative.
    </p>
    <p>As of the date on this page, Satsplain has:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>No affiliate links.</li>
      <li>No paid placements of another company's product.</li>
      <li>No sponsored posts.</li>
      <li>No commission when a reader opens an exchange, a wallet maker, or any other company.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Assume a link is not an affiliate link unless the page says, next to the link, that it is. If we add one, for example a link to a hardware-wallet maker, we will update this page first, name the relationship, and place a plain-language notice where the link appears, before a reader clicks. A fee would not change the rule that factual claims still need sources.
    </p>
    <p>We do not sell personal information. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
